radura","dish/serradura"],["Tocino de cielo","dish/tocino-de-cielo"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/2/25/Bacalhau_%C3%A0_minhota_edited.jpg/500px-Bacalhau_%C3%A0_minhota_edited.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"User:Adriao","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.5","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.5","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bacalhau_%C3%A0_minhota_edited.jpg"}},"dish/bajigur":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/bajigur","n":"Bajigur","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Bajigur is a hot and sweet beverage native to the Sundanese people of West Java, Indonesia. The main ingredients are coconut milk and Aren sugar; usually to add taste, a small amount of ginger and a small pinch of salt. Traditionally fragrant pandan leaves were added, but now often artificial vanilla powder is used. It can also include kopi tubruk, finely pounded coffee."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-bajigur"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bajigur"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Brown sugar","ingredient/brown-sugar"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Coffee","ingredient/coffee"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Palm sugar","ingredient/palm-sugar"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","ref":"site/dailycookingquest-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","dish/ayam-panggang"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-ta