oked with","count":2,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Cioppino","dish/cioppino"]]],["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine",[["Cioppino","dish/cioppino"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Clams","ingredient/clams"],["Dungeness crab","ingredient/dungeness-crab"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Mussel","ingredient/mussel"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Shrimp","ingredient/shrimp"],["Squid as food","ingredient/squid-as-food"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Tomatoes","ingredient/tomatoes"],["Wine","ingredient/wine"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/0/09/Argopecten_irradians.jpg/500px-Argopecten_irradians.jpg","w":500,"h":270,"by":"Rachael Norris and Marina Freudzon / Mayscallop at en.wikipedia","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Argopecten_irradians.jpg"}},"ingredient/grand-marnier":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/grand-marnier","n":"Grand Marnier","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Grand Marnier is a French brand of Curaçao liqueurs. The brand's best-known product is Grand Marnier Cordon Rouge, an orange-flavored liqueur created in 1880 by Alexandre Marnier-Lapostolle. It is made from a blend of Cognac brandy, distilled essence of bitter orange, and sugar, containing 40% alcohol (70 British proof/ 80 US proof).  It is commonly consumed \"neat\" as a cordial or a digestif, and can be used in mixed drinks and desserts. Popular examples of the latter include crêpes Suzette and crêpes au Grand Marnier."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-grand-marnier"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Marnier"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine",[["Crêpes Suzette","dish/crepes-suzette"]]],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine",[["Crêpe