ional soup."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-pork-jelly"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pork_jelly"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["English cuisine","cuisine/english-cuisine",[["Pork pie","dish/pork-pie"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Hot water crust pastry","ingredient/hot-water-crust-pastry"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"]]}]},"ingredient/sate-kambing":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/sate-kambing","n":"Sate kambing","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Sate kambing is the Indonesian name for \"mutton satay\". It is part of the cuisine of Indonesia. This food is made by grilling goat meat that has been mixed with seasoning. The dish is also called lamb satay and goat satay."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sate-kambing"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sate_kambing"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Sate klatak","dish/sate-klatak"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Candlenut","ingredient/candlenut"],["Caraway seed","ingredient/caraway-seed"],["Cinnamon","ingredient/cinnamon"],["Clove","ingredient/clove"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Galangal","ingredient/galangal"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Goat","ingredient/goat"],["Granulated sugar","ingredient/granulated-sugar"],["Gulai","ingredient/gulai"],["Lemongrass","ingredient/lemongrass"],["Lime","ingredient/lime"],["Margarine","ingredient/margarine"],["Sweet soy sauce","ingredient/sweet-soy-sauce"],["Tamarind","ingredient/tamarind"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/e2/Mutton_satay_from_H._Faqih%2C_Jombang%2C_2017-09-19_01.jpg/500px-Mutton_satay_from_H._Faqih%2C_Jombang%2C_2017-09-19_01.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Crisco 1492","lic":"CC 